    },
    "body": "**Lab 1 (Claude main). Class C** (`DECISIONS.md` and policy). **The owner decided it in the Lab 1 session**, answering four prompts, each with the recommended option, plus a synthesis instruction quoted verbatim in D12. References #820 and #973.\n\n- **`DECISIONS.md` D12:**\n  1. gates promote and never kill; parking a family needs a root-cause case and the owner's OK; D9 stays;\n  2. four geometric candidates are reopened with named next steps;\n  3. the native engine's mechanisms are ported into the stack's core: S4 (2I transport), then I1, prime/UOR keys, zeta phases;\n  4. S4 is judged three ways, with no kill;\n  5. a geometric toolbox.\n- **Policy:** a \"Gates promote; they never kill\" section. Recommend by the project's overall goal, not by the narrowest gate.\n- **ROADMAP:**\n  - **§5:** mechanism verdicts read \"not yet promoted\", and the kill rules are withdrawn.\n  - **§2a:** the porting track, the reopened candidates and an S4 row; D2 and D3 are relabeled.\n  - **§9:** a log entry.\n- **[Geometric toolbox](docs/integration/geometric-toolbox-2026-09-28.md):** every closed mechanism, sorted into four groups:\n  - **reopened:** the finite-group lanes (A5 exact, with a six-seed mean text cost of +0.018), exact memory, the geometric sparse index, trained-in read codes;\n  - **already in the main line:** the quaternion transport and Lorentz reads;\n  - **toolbox:** the 2I relation table, prime/CRT addressing and UOR identity, zeta phases, the exact Hopf map, E8/H4 codebooks, orthant admission, vector-symbolic binding, golden-ratio codebooks, horocycle and curvature, Cayley–Dickson algebra, the R4G1 kernel;\n  - **ordinary negatives.**\n\n  Each entry gives the capability shown, whether it is absent from the main line, a novelty assessment (Lab 1's, from known literature, with no result claimed), where the code lives, and what it could fix.\n- **Checks:** `check_claim_wording.py` passes.\n\n**Review:** a non-author accuracy check of the toolbox numbers against their sources follows before merge.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
